# tetron-relay host inventory.
#
# Copy this file to hosts.conf (gitignored -- your real infra is your own
# business) and edit. One host per line:
#
#   <name>  <target>
#
# <name> is a label used only within this tool (log lines, --host
# arguments) -- it does not need to match the real hostname.
#
# <target> is either the literal word "local" (run commands directly on
# this machine) or an SSH target (user@host, anything `ssh` itself accepts,
# including a Host alias from your own ~/.ssh/config). Unlike
# tetron-testsuite, every entry here is expected to be a real, persistent
# server you already provisioned -- not a disposable VM this tool creates.
# The SSH user needs passwordless sudo (or run as root directly) since
# bringup writes to /usr/local/bin, /etc/iroh-relay, and installs a
# systemd unit.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.

#relay-1  ssh:user@relay.example.com
